{
  "topic": "Your body's superpowers",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "Your BODY's Hidden SUPERPOWERS 🫀",
  "hook": "Your body has superpowers you use every day without noticing.",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_hook",
      "narration": "Your body has superpowers you use every day without noticing.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hidden superpowers",
      "highlight_words": [
        "superpowers"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_hook",
      "narration": "An engine that never stops, cameras that see upside down and prints nobody else in the world has.",
      "on_screen_text": "Engine, cameras and prints",
      "highlight_words": [
        "prints"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_hook",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and today I'll introduce you to the superpowers of your own body.",
      "on_screen_text": "Meet your body",
      "highlight_words": [
        "body"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_size",
      "narration": "First power: your heart. It's about the size of your fist, and it never rests.",
      "on_screen_text": "Fist-sized",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Fist-sized"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The engine"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_hook",
      "narration": "It beats about a hundred thousand times a day. Over a lifetime, billions of times.",
      "on_screen_text": "100,000 beats a day",
      "highlight_words": [
        "100,000"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_two",
      "narration": "It's really two pumps: the right side sends blood to the lungs and the left side to the rest of the body.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two pumps in one",
      "highlight_words": [
        "pumps"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_spark",
      "narration": "Each beat starts with a tiny electric spark, your natural pacemaker.",
      "on_screen_text": "A spark every beat",
      "highlight_words": [
        "spark"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_liters",
      "narration": "And every day it pumps about seven and a half thousand liters of blood. Enough to fill dozens of bathtubs.",
      "on_screen_text": "7,500 liters a day",
      "highlight_words": [
        "7,500"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_parts",
      "narration": "Second power: your eyes. They work like cameras, with a lens that focuses light onto the retina.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two cameras",
      "highlight_words": [
        "cameras"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The cameras"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_cells",
      "narration": "The retina has about a hundred and twenty million rods for dim light, and about six million cones for color.",
      "on_screen_text": "Millions of sensors",
      "highlight_words": [
        "sensors"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_flip",
      "narration": "Here's the twist: the image arrives upside down. Your brain flips it without you noticing.",
      "on_screen_text": "It all arrives upside down",
      "highlight_words": [
        "upside"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_blind",
      "narration": "And each eye has a blind spot, where the nerve leaves. Your brain fills that gap with what it guesses is there.",
      "on_screen_text": "The blind spot",
      "highlight_words": [
        "blind"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_blind",
      "narration": "You can find your blind spot by covering one eye and staring at a point while moving another object in from the side.",
      "on_screen_text": "Find your blind spot",
      "highlight_words": [
        "blind"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_saccade",
      "narration": "Your eyes jump about three times a second, and your brain erases those jumps so the picture doesn't shake.",
      "on_screen_text": "Invisible jumps",
      "highlight_words": [
        "jumps"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_ridges",
      "narration": "Third power: your fingerprints. They formed before you were born, between weeks ten and sixteen of pregnancy.",
      "on_screen_text": "Before birth",
      "highlight_words": [
        "birth"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The unique signature"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_twins",
      "narration": "Not even identical twins have the same fingerprints.",
      "on_screen_text": "Not even twins",
      "highlight_words": [
        "twins"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_touch",
      "narration": "And their ridges aren't just a pattern: they help you feel very fine textures as you slide your finger.",
      "on_screen_text": "A texture sensor",
      "highlight_words": [
        "texture"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_koala",
      "narration": "Surprise: koalas have fingerprints so similar to ours that they're hard to tell apart.",
      "on_screen_text": "Koalas with human prints!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Koalas"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_enamel",
      "narration": "Fourth power: the enamel on your teeth, the hardest material in your whole body.",
      "on_screen_text": "The hardest thing in you",
      "highlight_words": [
        "hardest"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The armor"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_norepair",
      "narration": "But it has a weak spot: it has no living cells, so it can't repair itself. That's why you need to look after it.",
      "on_screen_text": "It can't regrow",
      "highlight_words": [
        "regrow"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_count",
      "narration": "We have twenty baby teeth and up to thirty-two adult ones, waiting hidden in the jaw.",
      "on_screen_text": "20 + 32 teeth",
      "highlight_words": [
        "32"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_body",
      "narration": "All these systems work together, day and night, without you having to think about them.",
      "on_screen_text": "A perfect team",
      "highlight_words": [
        "team"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_body",
      "narration": "Your blood vessels, laid end to end, would wrap around Earth several times. Your heart pushes blood through all of them nonstop.",
      "on_screen_text": "A huge journey",
      "highlight_words": [
        "journey"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_valves",
      "narration": "The famous thump-thump you hear is the sound of your heart valves closing.",
      "on_screen_text": "The sound of valves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "valves"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_lungs",
      "narration": "In the lungs, blood drops off carbon dioxide and picks up fresh oxygen.",
      "on_screen_text": "Fresh oxygen",
      "highlight_words": [
        "oxygen"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_squeeze",
      "narration": "When you run, it can beat twice as fast to bring more oxygen to your muscles.",
      "on_screen_text": "Faster when you run",
      "highlight_words": [
        "run"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_pupil",
      "narration": "The pupil widens in the dark and shrinks in bright light, like a camera's aperture.",
      "on_screen_text": "The pupil adjusts",
      "highlight_words": [
        "pupil"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_colors",
      "narration": "With just three types of cones, your brain mixes signals and tells apart a huge number of colors.",
      "on_screen_text": "Three cones, countless colors",
      "highlight_words": [
        "colors"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_patterns",
      "narration": "There are three basic fingerprint patterns: arches, loops and whorls. Which one do you have?",
      "on_screen_text": "Arches, loops, whorls",
      "highlight_words": [
        "whorls"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_police",
      "narration": "That's why police have used them for more than a century to identify people.",
      "on_screen_text": "A lifelong signature",
      "highlight_words": [
        "signature"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s31",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_roots",
      "narration": "When an adult tooth comes in, the baby tooth's root dissolves, and that's why it falls out.",
      "on_screen_text": "Why they fall out",
      "highlight_words": [
        "fall"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s32",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_cavity",
      "narration": "Bacteria turn sugar into acid, and that acid is what damages enamel.",
      "on_screen_text": "Sugar + bacteria = acid",
      "highlight_words": [
        "acid"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ojo_rays",
      "narration": "Light enters through the pupil, the lens focuses it and the retina turns it into electrical signals for the brain.",
      "on_screen_text": "Light turned into signals",
      "highlight_words": [
        "signals"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s34",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_unique",
      "narration": "Fingerprints don't change over your lifetime: if you cut yourself, the skin grows back with the same pattern.",
      "on_screen_text": "The same pattern forever",
      "highlight_words": [
        "pattern"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_shark",
      "narration": "Sharks, on the other hand, replace their teeth again and again, and can go through thousands in a lifetime.",
      "on_screen_text": "Sharks with spares",
      "highlight_words": [
        "spares"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s36",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "die_jaw",
      "narration": "Adult teeth form hidden in your jaw while you're still using your baby teeth.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hidden in the jaw",
      "highlight_words": [
        "jaw"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s37",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_hook",
      "narration": "So next time you look in the mirror, remember: you're looking at a superhero.",
      "on_screen_text": "You're a superhero",
      "highlight_words": [
        "superhero"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s38",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_outro",
      "narration": "Which part of the body should we explore next? Tell me in the comments.",
      "on_screen_text": "Which part is next?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "part"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A heart that beats 100,000 times a day, eyes that see upside down, a blind spot your brain fills in, unique fingerprints and the hardest material in your body. Verified facts, explained in 3D. Original 3D animation; sizes and distances are not to scale.",
